DESCRIPTIONS = {
    "Hydrogel": "A hydrogel is a soft, jelly-like dressing that is mostly water. It keeps the wound moist, which supports healing, and it feels cooling and is gentle to remove. It absorbs only a small amount of fluid, so it suits dry or lightly weeping wounds and minor burns better than heavily leaking wounds.",
    "Alginate": "Alginate dressings are made from seaweed. They soak up a lot of wound fluid and turn into a soft gel, which helps keep the wound moist. This makes them a good choice for wounds that leak a lot, but they can cost more and are not suitable for dry wounds.",
    "Chitosan": "Chitosan comes from the shells of crabs and shrimp. It is known for helping to stop bleeding and for slowing the growth of bacteria. It has a medium level of absorbency, and it can be more costly. People with shellfish allergies should be careful with it.",
}
